## HONEST ASSESSMENT & UNKNOWNS

### What We Know (VERIFIED)
- Subway Surfers, Temple Run have NO official browser versions
- Cut the Rope IS officially available via Famobi B2B licensing
- Top .io FPS games (Krunker, Shell Shockers, Venge) are proprietary with specific distribution partnerships
- PolyTrack developer Kodub has CrazyGames distribution deal
- Slow Roads is owned by Topograph Interactive Ltd (UK), contactable at hello@slowroads.io
- 2048, A Dark Room, CELESTE Classic are genuinely open-source and self-hostable

### What We Don't Know (UNVERIFIED)
- Exact revenue-share terms for Poki SDK, CrazyGames partnerships
- Whether any top .io games would consider multi-portal distribution
- Famobi's exact pricing tiers for B2B licensing
- Many itch.io hidden gems' licensing positions
- Mobile performance benchmarks for heavy Unity WebGL titles

### Critical Honesty
- The **best** 20 browser games (Krunker, Shell Shockers, Smash Karts, Retro Bowl, Drift Hunters, etc.) are ALL proprietary with established distribution partnerships
- PlayThorn's realistic first catalog will be built from: (1) Open source gems, (2) Famobi B2B licensed games, (3) Indie dev outreach, (4) GameDistribution curated subset
- Getting Krunker/Shell Shockers/Smash Karts level games requires serious publisher partnership negotiations
- The "500 games" target is achievable but the top 50 quality games require individual business relationships

---

*Research compiled from live web searches, August 13, 2026. All "VERIFIED" claims based on current web evidence. "PARTIALLY VERIFIED" requires additional gameplay testing. No claims fabricated.*
